==Overview==
<tabber>
|-|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* High combo potential.
* High damage on all moves.
* Good mobility.
* Not too difficult to obtain compared to other {{Mythical}} fruits.
* Pairs perfectly with [[Godhuman]] or [[Sanguine Art]].
* Pairs very well with the [[Cyborg]] race.
* Moves can drain lots of [[Instinct]] if dodged.

|'''[Z] Somber Rebellion'''
* Can be used to escape combos (if timed correctly), as it flings the user into the air.
* Decent speed.
* Great for combo starting.
* Good to avoid other attacks like [[Gravity Blade]]'s [Z] move or [[Portal]]'s [Z] move as it gives I-frame protection.

|'''[X] Shade Nest'''
* The bats have auto-aim and will fly towards the target if they're not too far away.
* Good range.
* Can stun enemies.
* Little to no endlag.

|'''[C] Nightmare Leech'''
* Heals the user by 20% of their max [[health]] when PvP, which can be extremely useful when the player is low on [[health]].
* Kills [[Pain]] and [[Ghost]] users before they revive.
* Breaks [[Instinct]] no matter what.
* Can be used almost exactly like [[Sanguine Art]]s [Z] move, but with more endlag.
* Briefly stuns opponents.

|'''[V] Corvus Torment'''
* Very high damage.
* Relatively low cooldown, especially considering its strength.
* Huge hitbox, [[AoE]], and stun especially when used with full Umbra Meter.
* Great for grinding, as most [[Enemies]] will not escape the explosion.
* Drains [[Instinct]] if dodged.
* Great combo potential if the victim is trapped inside.

|'''[F] Umbrage'''
* Great for grinding and pairs really well with [[Cyborg]] V3 ([[Energy Core]]).
** This can be used to hold players inside of the [V].
* Makes the user's hitbox extremely small, making it useful for evasion in many situations.
* Extremely high damage if fully held.
}}
|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* High mastery requirements.
* Passive quite inconvenient during the day.
* Bad for some [[Sea Events]].
* Moves are hard to hit, all needing at least a stun to hit in PvP.
* Moves can be [[Instinct]]-tricked.

|'''[Z] Somber Rebellion'''
* Single target.
* Small hitbox.
* Sends the user upwards, which sometimes can be annoying for starting/extending a combo.

|'''[X] Shade Nest'''
* Relatively slow speed.
* Small hitbox.
* Unlikely to break [[Instinct]] due to it needing precise aim.
* Mostly single-target. (Unless aimed differently.)

|'''[C] Nightmare Leech'''
* Single target.
* Low range, along with end-lag if the user misses.
* While it 'can' kill [[Pain]] and [[Ghost]] users, the move has short range and significant endlag.
* Longer than average end-lag.
* No I-frames, meaning the user can be damaged by an enemy if using the move on something already.

|'''[V] Corvus Torment'''
* Most players can escape the explosion's radius, making it almost impossible to deal full damage in PvP without a proper stun/holder.
* Doesn't break [[Instinct]].
* Quite small [[AoE]] if Umbra Meter isn't full.

|'''[F] Umbrage'''
* Can only be held for 10 seconds, making it less reliable for mobility.
* Slow flight speed.
* Not viable for PvP.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Shadow was the only fruit that allows the user to utilize the life drain mechanic (just like [[Ghoul]]'s life leech) by using {{Ability|C}}.
* It is one of the only fruits that have wings on their physical fruit model, along with [[Eagle]], [[Spirit]] and [[Phoenix]]. 
* "Umbra" in Latin means "shade" and/or "shadow", and "Corvus" in Latin refers to a raven or a crow, both being types of birds. This ties into how many of the fruit's abilities have to do with crows/ravens flying at the enemy.
* Shadow's [Z], [X], [C] moves are quite similar to [[Godhuman]]'s [Z], [X] (Tap Variant) and [C], having nearly identical range, cooldowns, and energy usage.
* Shadow is the rarest and most expensive fruit obtainable from a [[Fruit Box]].
* Shadow does not construct the user's body out of shadows, but rather, uses them in the form of attacks, hence why Shadow isn't [[Elemental]], but rather a [[Natural]] [[Blox Fruits|fruit]]. 
* Despite its physical appearance resembling a bat, the attacks use crows.
* Shadow’s [C] is the only move with a finisher that makes the target burst on contact. Shadow and [[Dragon Talon]] are also the only abilities with finisher‑style variants in the game.
* Shadows [V] move is the only [V] move of a [[Mythical]] fruit that can be dodged no matter what. However, its damage and stun makes it extremely deadly if hit.
** Interestingly, Shadow, [[Diamond]], and [[Awakenings Expert|Awakened]] [[Light]] are the only [[Blox Fruits]] thats [V] move can be dodged no matter what with [[Instinct]].
* Shadow is confirmed to be getting a rework in future updates.
* Interestingly, if user used {{Ability|V}} while a [[Ghost]] user uses {{Ability|Ghost|V}}, they would be able to see the darkness effect from the [V] move and see how it can invert colours and create darkness, and lasts until the move ends.

